- [Expand a cluster](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-update-broker-count.md): Increase the number of brokers in an Amazon MSK cluster using the AWS Management Console, the AWS CLI, or the API.
- [Remove a broker](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-remove-broker.md): Increase the number of brokers in an Amazon MSK cluster using the AWS Management Console, the AWS CLI, or the API.
- [Update cluster broker size](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-update-broker-type.md): Update the Amazon MSK cluster broker size for all the brokers in the cluster using the AWS Management Console, the AWS CLI, or the API.
- [Use Cruise Control](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/cruise-control.md): How to use Cruise Control to rebalance and monitor your Amazon MSK cluster.
- [Update cluster configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-update-cluster-config.md): Update the configuration of a Amazon MSK clustercluster.
- [Configure dual-stack network type](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/mskp-choose-cluster-network-type.md): Configure IPv4 or dual-stack network type for your MSK Provisioned clusters.
- [Reboot a broker for an Amazon MSK cluster](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-reboot-broker.md): Reboot a broker for an Amazon MSK cluster using the AWS Management Console, the AWS CLI, or the API.

